    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d865">

                <pb facs="0796" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R.–Subs/19</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornibrook</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2355</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-13">July 13,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received July 22.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s circular telegram of June 13, 8 p.m., concerning the possible
                    adoption by the American Republics of a uniform policy with regard to the
                    exclusion of belligerent submarines from the ports and territorial waters of
                    these republics, and to inform the Department that this matter was brought to
                    the attention of the Minister of Foreign Affairs on June 14. <pb facs="0797"
                        n="785" xml:id="pg785"/> After subsequently pressing several times for a
                    reply, the Minister informed the Legation in a note dated July 1 that the matter
                    had been referred to the Ministry of Public Security for consideration. Nothing
                    further on the subject has been heard from the Foreign Office since that
                    time.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. H. Hornibrook</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
